# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# bin/ and obj/ are the ones that matter. Copying a host build into the image poisons the
# restore: NuGet finds project.assets.json from a Windows SDK and the Linux publish either
# reuses the wrong graph or fails outright. They are also, by a distance, the largest thing
# in this repository.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Local build outputs from the scratch harnesses — bo-api, bo-web and friends.
bo-*/

# Not built here, and 60 MB of Python besides.
PMS_Python/

# The Dockerfile copies only src/. These are listed anyway so `docker build` does not ship them
# to the daemon in the first place.
tests/
tools/
docs/
database/

# Secrets and local overrides. appsettings.Development.json is excluded deliberately: the
# container is configured by environment variable, and baking a developer's connection string
# into an image is how a production container ends up pointed at a laptop.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
.env
*.pfx
*.key

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
**/README.md
**/*.log
